+/*
+ * Apotheosis (WK_WINUWP): Windows 10 Mobile / App Container media backend.
+ *
+ * This file is WebKit-WinUWP-only and is compiled from PlatformWinUWP.cmake and
+ * nothing else (same convention as platform/graphics/texmap/TextureMapperTileGridStore.*).
+ *
+ * WHY NOT platform/graphics/win/MediaPlayerPrivateMediaFoundation.*:
+ *   Upstream's Media Foundation backend is written for Win32 desktop. It builds an
+ *   EVR topology (MFCreateTopology + Direct3DPresenter on D3D9 with an HWND, DComp,
+ *   DXVA2 display mode) and presents straight into a desktop window surface. In an
+ *   App Container there is no HWND to present into and no D3D9 swap chain we can own;
+ *   the harness presents through either Cairo paintToRGBA or the TextureMapper/ANGLE
+ *   SwapChainPanel path. So the *decode* half of Media Foundation is reusable and the
+ *   *presentation* half is not.
+ *
+ * DESIGN:
+ *   MFCreateSourceReaderFromURL -> IMFSourceReader with the Video Processor MFT
+ *   auto-inserted (MF_SOURCE_READER_ENABLE_VIDEO_PROCESSING), asked for RGB32 output.
+ *   Every decoded video sample is converted into a plain CPU BGRA buffer; the page
+ *   then paints it through the ordinary GraphicsContext::drawNativeImage path, which
+ *   means the software (Cairo) and GPU (TextureMapper) presentation routes both get
+ *   the frame for free and no new present path is introduced.
+ *
+ *   Audio samples are converted to interleaved float32 and pushed into the platform's
+ *   PCM queue through WinUWPMediaAudioSink. That interface is declared here and
+ *   *implemented by the platform layer* (port/), so the dependency points inward:
+ *   WebCore never references a port/ symbol.
+ *
+ * THREADING (the port's single-engine-thread rule):
+ *   All Media Foundation calls, including creating the source reader, happen on one
+ *   dedicated decode thread owned by this object. That thread never calls into
+ *   MediaPlayer: it publishes frames into a double buffer and then hops to the engine
+ *   thread with callOnMainThread() before notifying anything, which is the same
+ *   post-to-the-run-loop route the loader already uses. No new synchronization point
+ *   is introduced and the engine thread is never made to wait for media.
+ */
+
